---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import UpdateBadge from '../../components/UpdateBadge.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import SourceList from '../../components/SourceList.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import AdsterraBanner300x250 from '../../components/AdsterraBanner300x250.astro';
import { sourceUrls, patch107, patch109, patch110, latestAppliedPatch, previousApplied, patch111Preview, plannedUpdate11 } from '../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Roadmap: Latest Updates & Future Plans';
const description = 'DragonSword Awakening Version 1.1 is scheduled for October 15 with Ryza, Hunt updates, Training Ground, costumes and QoL; 1.0.12 remains latest applied.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/roadmap/';
const article = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-10-04', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' } };
const sources = [
  { label: 'Official LIVE STREAM #7 replay', href: plannedUpdate11.replayHref, note: 'Evidence B — official replay with creator-provided English and Japanese captions; gives the October 15 Version 1.1 target and showcased scope. It is not an applied-update notice.' },
  { label: 'Official 1.1 livestream notice', href: plannedUpdate11.noticeHref, note: 'Evidence B — confirms the official showcase scope and identifies Version 1.1 as upcoming.' },
  { label: 'Official Ryza teaser announcement', href: 'https://steamcommunity.com/games/4570720/announcements/detail/1844115010490208', note: 'Evidence B — published September 17, 2026 KST (September 16 UTC); announces her October arrival.' },
  { label: 'Official post-launch roadmap & Q&A', href: sourceUrls.roadmap, note: 'Evidence B — primary roadmap source for post-launch plans, heroes, Rifts, multiplayer Raids and platform status.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.12', href: latestAppliedPatch.href, note: 'Evidence B — latest applied patch; published September 10, 2026 KST.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.11', href: previousApplied.href, note: 'Evidence B — previous applied patch; published September 3, 2026 KST.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.10', href: patch110.href, note: 'Evidence B — historical applied patch; published August 19, 2026.' },
  { label: 'Official 1.0.11 patch preview (historical)', href: patch111Preview.href, note: 'Evidence B — historical announcement source; its separate Coming Next items are not classified as applied 1.0.11 content.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} routeId="roadmap" ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Roadmap' }]} /><article>
    <header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Updates · Source timeline</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Roadmap</h1><LastVerified date="October 4, 2026" /></header>
    <div class="roadmap-hero"><UpdateBadge label={`${plannedUpdate11.label} · ${plannedUpdate11.date}`} href={plannedUpdate11.replayHref} /><h2>Follow the official trail, not rumor.</h2><p>Version 1.1 has an official October 15, 2026 target from LIVE STREAM #7. It has not yet been confirmed applied; Update 1.0.12 remains the latest applied patch.</p></div>
    <QuickAnswer title="Version 1.1 is scheduled for October 15; 1.0.12 remains the latest applied update."><p>The official replay schedules Ryza, Hunt Rank and Hell Difficulty, the Training Ground, Othello Hero Quest, three costumes and listed quality-of-life changes for Version 1.1. This is an official target, not an applied-release notice.</p></QuickAnswer>
    <AdsterraNativeBanner/>
    <div class="timeline"><div><span class="date">Latest applied / released</span><h2>1.0.12 applied</h2><p>Steam published the applied Update Notes on September 10, 2026 KST.</p></div><div><span class="date">Released / previous</span><h2>1.0.11 applied</h2><p><a href={previousApplied.href}>1.0.11 remains the previous applied patch</a>; <a href={patch109.href}>1.0.9 is earlier release history</a>.</p></div><div><span class="date">Scheduled / not yet applied</span><h2>Version 1.1 target: October 15, 2026</h2><p>LIVE STREAM #7 gives October 15 as the target. Until official update notes confirm application, Version 1.1 remains scheduled.</p></div></div>
    <section class="roadmap-details"><h2>Latest applied / released: 1.0.12</h2><p>The official applied notes list these fixes:</p><ul><li>Localization corrections to Aria’s Bomb Arrows attack-count description and Theresia’s costume weapon description.</li><li>Astria’s Slide no longer receives an unintended cooldown after learning Blazing Lightning, and the hero can rotate while using Slide.</li><li>Fixes for abnormal Super Armor during Andras the Cave Predator’s ceiling-hanging pattern, unintended invincibility when switching coincides with a hit-induced Familiar dismount, and a 5-Star Equipment crafting result popup that could not be closed after the cinematic finished.</li></ul><h2>Released / previous: 1.0.11</h2><p>The final official Update Notes confirm these applied areas:</p><ul><li>Just Dodge, including its documented invincibility, guaranteed-critical, Active Skill Rage and Dodge Stamina effects.</li><li>Lock-On control, retention, target-search and camera improvements.</li><li>A one-second Super Armor protection for the Hero left on the field after switching.</li><li>Balance changes for Lute, Aria, Tarte, Roxy, Astria, Kalsion and Dana.</li><li>Multiplayer Retry, fastest-response lobby search, version notices, lobby fixes and departure notifications.</li><li>System quality-of-life work, localization corrections and listed bug fixes.</li></ul><p class="evidence-note"><strong>Final-notes boundary:</strong> these applied claims come from the final 1.0.11 Update Notes, not merely from the earlier preview.</p><h2>Release history: 1.0.10</h2><ul><li>Update 1.0.10 remains a historical applied release dated August 19, 2026.</li><li><a href={patch107.href}>1.0.7</a> remains historical context for Quick Entry, the former matching-range setting, map pins and Rune changes.</li></ul><h2>Version 1.1 / scheduled, not yet applied</h2><p>LIVE STREAM #7 gives an October 15, 2026 target for Version 1.1 and confirms this scheduled scope:</p><ul><li>Ryza (Playable Hero) — Quest #53, “Reunion,” grants her as its completion reward; players who already completed that story point are scheduled to receive her directly in their inventory when the update goes live.</li><li>Othello Hero Quest — scheduled with Version 1.1.</li><li>Hunt Hell Difficulty — scheduled alongside a Hunt Rank system on every difficulty, with ranks from D through S.</li><li>Training Ground — a practice space entered through Edric at Orbis Castle, with stationary, moving and multi-target training options plus damage and DPS readouts.</li><li>Quality-of-life changes — Quick Slots increase from two to three; cooking cooldown and ingredient display changes; more Map Pin icon types; a Tag Combo Animation toggle; Familiar-menu acquisition improvements; and in-play achievement completion notices.</li><li>Costumes — three costumes, for Eileen, Othello and Reina.</li></ul><p class="evidence-note"><strong>Schedule boundary:</strong> the replay states an October 15 target and says a more detailed schedule will follow through official channels. Until final update notes confirm application, all Version 1.1 items remain scheduled rather than released.</p><h2>Later / date unknown</h2><ul><li>Earlier official roadmap material also names Jerome, Veronica and Logan as planned Heroes, alongside broader Hero Quest, Rift and multiplayer Raid direction. Their dependable release dates remain unknown.</li><li>The roadmap does not establish a current console launch date, cross-platform play or story/open-world co-op.</li></ul><p class="evidence-note"><strong>Evidence B boundary:</strong> the roadmap, official Steam announcements and official replay are primary sources. Community pages may help identify questions, but they do not upgrade a feature, date, platform or character claim.</p><AdsterraBanner300x250/><p>For current system changes, continue to the <a href="/systems/runes/">Rune guide</a> or the <a href="/builds/">build framework</a>; those pages own their narrower intents.</p></section>
    <SourceList sources={sources} />
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.page-wrap{padding:1.25rem 0 2rem}.article-header{max-width:820px;margin-bottom:1.5rem}.eyebrow{color:var(--accent-light);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}h1,h2{line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.04em}h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,7vw,5rem);margin:0 0 .7rem}h2{font-size:clamp(1.45rem,3vw,2rem);margin:.8rem 0 .45rem}.roadmap-hero{padding:1.5rem;background:linear-gradient(115deg,var(--accent-soft),var(--paper));border:1px solid hsl(199 86% 58% / .35);border-radius:14px}.roadmap-hero p{max-width:60ch;color:var(--muted-strong)}.timeline{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem;margin:2.5rem 0}.timeline>div{border-top:1px solid var(--accent);padding-top:1rem}.timeline h2{margin:.35rem 0;font-size:1.3rem}.timeline p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem}.date{color:var(--accent-light);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}@media(max-width:700px){.timeline{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
